  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "steer-steps-provenance-ablate",
    "parent": "steer-preference-denominator-counter",
    "kind": "ablate",
    "title": "Test whether steerAuthority.steps is an independent count or an alias of termination.stepsUsedSum",
    "description": "steerAuthority.steps has now matched termination.stepsUsedSum to the digit across four sequential runs, which is consistent with the counter being incremented at the budget-decrement site rather than at the steer decision site. In spur-core/src/simulator/core/scheduler.rs, move/duplicate the increment so that steerAuthority.steps is incremented only inside the block that actually reaches the steer decision point, and add steerAuthority.stepsTotal incremented at the existing (budget) site. Extend spur-core/tests/steer_authority_wiring.rs to assert steps <= stepsTotal and to fail if steps == stepsTotal for a run where at least one step short-circuits before the decision point. Re-run general_vr.json and report the ratio steps/stepsTotal. No policy change, no new config field. Depends on the export-parity fix landing first so stepsTotal is actually visible.",
    "category": "tooling",
    "buildsOn": [
      "scheduler step loop",
      "util_stats",
      "steer-stats-export-parity-test"
    ],
    "expectedGain": 3,
    "expectedCost": 1,
    "rationale": "If steps is instrumenting the budget decrement rather than the steer site, then the parent rewire's 'falsifier passed' was a false green and every zero downstream is explained by the decision site simply not being on the hot path. Separating the two counts decides that in one run.",
    "generalityArgument": "Distinguishes two increment sites in the scheduler's own step loop; keyed on control flow only, no protocol-specific entity referenced.",
    "status": "proposed",
    "branch": null,
    "prUrls": [],
    "createdAtIso": "2026-08-29T23:45:00Z",
    "firingCounter": null,
    "notes": "[unparked iteration 5349] The denominator now matters (expression is 2.7e-5/step); steps=4808048 equals queue_audit_skipped exactly and is 1/3 of preference_consulted, so the alias question is live and cheap; falsified if steps < stepsTotal strictly after the split."
  },
